"""Package the coordinate experiment after all measurements and writers have stopped.

This script never fetches, changes the worktree, stages into a real index, replaces
an existing output directory, or follows evidence symlinks. It needs Linux,
Python 3.10+, and Git. Its temporary Git objects and indexes are deleted after
verification. Atomic publication uses Linux renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE).

Typical invocation (run only AFTER measurements):

    python3 result-coordinate-evidence/package-coordinate-deliverables.py \
        --report result-coordinate-evidence/final-report.md \
        --manifest result-coordinate-evidence/delivery-selection.json

Optional JSON selection manifest; entries are exact repository-relative files,
except evidence_roots, which are repository-relative directories:

    {
      "source_include": ["result-coordinate-evidence/extra-driver.py"],
      "evidence_roots": ["result-coordinate-evidence"],
      "evidence_include": ["initial-evidence.txt"],
      "reports": ["result-coordinate-evidence/final-report.md"]
    }

Tracked superproject files and all nonignored new files under
core/sail/lmdb/src are always selected, subject to the documented exclusions.
Other untracked source files require an explicit selection or a default task-file
entry below. Initialized submodules are recursively included from clean tracked
worktrees. Missing submodules fail by default; the explicit opt-out records an
incomplete external-source boundary and must not be used to claim a fully
vendored project. No network access is performed.

The evidence archive includes task logs/data/reports and small supporting text,
but excludes copied build artifacts, frozen object trees, stores, recordings,
credentials, and heaps. Every included entry has a verified SHA-256 inventory.
Both archives extract under rdf4j/ so repository-relative report links work when
the source and evidence archives are extracted into the same directory.
"""

